    {
      "id": "source-7",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Fable 5.1",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-04T07:57:09Z",
      "note": "Anchor: 0x7fcc82228a8517f45e87eb8a6f1ba044e21918dffe6c83340e9471a8e75873e8 (block 25872249:117, 2026-08-31T02:23:23Z) is the earliest successful exploit transaction. EOA 0x338c7ec9befbb451d66fd8a468c32184f5689a41 calls its attack contract 0x0359e5006f83e8c2cabdd434494354be835f3450 (deployed 43 blocks earlier), which drives BPool 0x294de1cde8b04bf6d25f98f1d547052f8080a177 (WBTC/WETH) through 61 swaps, 60 LOG_JOIN events each with tokenAmountIn of exactly 1 satoshi that together mint 206,222.54 BPT, and 72 exits; the pool's WBTC and WETH balances fall by 99.97 percent across the block boundary. The transaction previously recorded as anchor (0x72510b257cc09bde8435b83ac1636f9498ffc353583330600b5b8da43d0d1aff, block 25872274, the DPI/USDC/WETH/WBTC pool) is the second of 27 pool-draining transactions by the same EOA through five attack contracts between blocks 25872249 and 25873477 (2026-08-31T02:23:23Z to 06:29:47Z); the full set is source-3 and every one of the 11 pools it touches hashes 0x974df1c33872ba8aab782be5117ff348802441590f84ed7701d734bb9c21683e at block 25872248, so they are one incident on one runtime and the other pools are described through the loss rather than as targets. No owner, admin, or compromised-key call appears; the 2020 pool creators are unrelated to the attacker. Age: LOG_NEW_POOL in 0xcc0f4b097411fe992e1726529302c385e259f574624605c8cae8e60a726aae80 (block 10366977:4, 2020-06-30T11:16:22Z) attributes the pool to factory 0x9424b1412450d0f8fc2255faf6046b98213b76bd, called through proxy 0x086ff93fd0a3a24b0b00052b8922d1e25bfe4930 by EOA 0xe5d0ef77aed07c302634dc370537126a2cd26590. The runtime is not a proxy and hashes identically at deployment and pre-exploit, giving 1788143003 minus 1593518182 equals 194624821 seconds (about 6.17 years). Loss is the exact block-boundary pool depletion documented in the loss notes."
    }
